; Scrub — 1st Scrub terrain visual (habitat-tiers ruling, 2026-09-04 -> task-8-brief.md).
; Emits `browse` + `rocks` (project/data/terrain/scrub.tres). `browse` vs Grass/Meadow's
; `open_grass` is the real ecological browser/grazer split; this is the "wild grass with
; tags" the human described, distinct from — and NOT a change to — wild_grass.tres itself,
; which stays deliberately inert.
;
; Sources:
;   - Rock_1.fbx — REUSED, no new download. Already imported at
;     res://assets/terrain/rock_1/Rock_1.fbx (Ultimate Nature Pack, Quaternius, CC0) and
;     already recorded in quaternius_ultimate_nature_pack.tres's assets_used — referenced
;     here directly by uid rather than instancing Rock1.tscn's own wrapper, same "reuse the
;     raw piece, not the sibling terrain's full wrapper" convention RockCluster1.tscn
;     already established for this exact file.
;   - Bush_Common_Flowers.gltf, Fern_1.gltf, Grass_Wispy_Short.gltf — NEWLY imported this
;     pass, Stylized Nature MegaKit (Standard/free), Quaternius, CC0 1.0 Universal.
;     License.txt re-checked per asset-import-pipeline.md's audit gate before import (same
;     boilerplate CC0 1.0 text as every other use of this pack). Recorded in
;     project/attribution/sources/quaternius_stylized_nature_megakit.tres.
;
; COMPOSITION: a dry olive/tan slab (Color(0.58, 0.52, 0.34, 1) — deliberately distinct from
; Grass/Meadow's green and Forest's dark green, reading as rough/dry ground rather than
; lawn) carries 1x Rock_1 (the `rocks` visual source) + 1x Bush_Common_Flowers + 1x Fern_1
; (the woody/browse-able foliage a browser eats, as opposed to Meadow/Grass's open grass
; blades) + 2x Grass_Wispy_Short (sparse, scrubby ground texture, distinct from the denser
; MultiMesh lawn treatment Grass/Meadow use).
;
; SCALE: all 4 raw meshes measured via a one-off SceneTree AABB probe (same procedure prior
; passes used). Rock_1 uses the same 0.25 scale RockCluster1.tscn's Rock_A piece uses (raw
; height 0.87775, well-established "small scattered rock" target). Bush_Common_Flowers raw
; height 1.581786 -> scaled 0.3793 (target ~0.6 tile-units, matching Bush.tscn's established
; "ground-level shrub" class). Fern_1 raw height 0.840243 (footprint a wide 2.83x2.65,
; already a pre-clustered clump in the source file, not a single frond) -> scaled 0.4165
; (target ~0.35 tile-units height; footprint at this scale ~1.18x1.10, comparable overhang
; to a canopy tree's). Grass_Wispy_Short raw height 1.071847 -> scaled 0.14 (target ~0.15
; tile-units, a hair taller than Grass's ~0.10 lawn baseline to read as coarser/wispier).
; FIRST-PASS PROPOSAL, no GDD number exists for any of these — FLAG FOR HUMAN SIGN-OFF, same
; open posture as every prior prop-scale call in this codebase.
;
; SINGLE VARIANT: ships with exactly one `model_scenes` entry — same posture as Meadow.tscn
; and every terrain's first pass; a multi-variant richness pass is out of scope here.
;
; EVERYTHING GROUND-LEVEL NESTED UNDER ONE NODE NAMED "Slab" (OcclusionFader exemption
; convention, see CommonTree1.tscn's header); the 4 prop instances sit as plain siblings of
; Slab, same as every other terrain wrapper in this codebase.
[gd_scene load_steps=6 format=3]

